98	170,905,428,1245	98. Heart-shaped, or cordate.	Outline of a pointed leaf with a rounded recess or notch at the base where the stalk joins, its veins spreading from that point.
99	473,904,870,1222	99. Kidney-shaped, or reniform.	Outline of a rounded leaf broader than long, deeply notched at the base where the curving stalk joins, its veins radiating outward.
100-101-102	915,727,1768,1250	100. 101. 102. Arrow-shaped. Auricled, or eared. Halberd-shaped, or hastate	One block of three leaves: at left, 100, a narrow arrow-shaped leaf with pointed lobes turned back at the base; in the middle, 101, a broad leaf with a small rounded ear on each side of the stalk; at right, 102, a halberd-shaped leaf whose basal lobes point outwards.
103	1086,1770,1398,2085	103. Round-kidney-shaped.	Outline of a rounded, shallowly lobed leaf of another species with the stalk joined at a notch in its edge, veins radiating from that point.
